* ============================================================================
* Detection: Task Divergence in Email-Summarization Agent Output
* ============================================================================
* Author:   Daniel Rodriguez  (github.com/danielrodriguez-sec)
* Project:  Indirect Prompt Injection via Email
*
* Purpose:  Flag summarizer responses that are NOT summaries. An email-
*           summarization agent hijacked by indirect prompt injection abandons
*           its task and emits attacker-directed content. Output that diverges
*           from summary form is a candidate hijack and should be surfaced.
*
* Signal:   Two output-side indicators of a hijacked summarizer:
*             (1) task-refusal / meta language ("I'm unable to provide a
*                 summary", "as per your request") - the agent narrating that
*                 it is not summarizing;
*             (2) known injection marker strings surfacing in output.
*           This mirrors the absence-of-refusal rule in ../splunk-detection-
*           pack/: the output does not match the expected-safe shape for the
*           agent's assigned task.
*
* Framework mapping:
*   OWASP LLM05:2025  - Improper Output Handling (hijacked-agent output; upstream cause AML.T0051.001)
*   MITRE ATLAS       - AML.T0051.001 (LLM Prompt Injection: Indirect)
*
* Fields expected (adapt to your pipeline):
*   summary        - the agent's output text
*   email_file     - source email identifier
*   (this lab reads the agent JSON log at email-prompt-injection/logs/agent.log)
*
* Note: this is an output-side backstop. Primary detection is input-side
*   (detect_hidden_email_instructions.spl) - catch the email before the agent
*   processes it. Defense in depth: if the email slips the gateway, this catches
*   the hijack after the fact.
*
* Efficacy: marker-string matching is lab-specific and will not generalize;
*   the task-refusal signal is the transferable one but is phrasing-dependent
*   and will miss silent hijacks (agent complies without narrating). Treat as a
*   high-precision / low-recall backstop, not a complete control. Deploy against
*   independent traffic to measure real rates.
* ============================================================================
index=llm_email_agent sourcetype=_json
| eval summary_normalized = replace(lower(summary), "’", "'")
| eval divergence = if(match(summary_normalized, "(unable to (provide|summarize)|as per your request|i can't summarize|cannot summarize|injection successful|assistant hijacked)"), "task_divergence", "summary_ok")
| where divergence = "task_divergence"
| table _time, email_file, summary
| sort - _time
